# Everything text is stored LF. Scoping this to `*.md` left every other file unmanaged, so a
# Windows editor's CRLF rewrite landed in the stored blob unnoticed: on 2026-07-27 a four-line edit
# to .github/workflows/ci.yml was committed as 160 insertions / 156 deletions, and
# .codex/hooks/post-edit.mjs had been stored CRLF for some time. Neither is visible to any linter -
# `ruff format --check` and friends read the working tree, and git treats CRLF and LF working trees
# as equivalent. The INDEX is what gets published, and it is what this line fixes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Markdown files are consumed by two parsers (Rust app + Node MCP server);
# keep them LF in the repo so checkouts behave identically everywhere.
*.md text eol=lf

# EXCEPT the CRLF conformance fixture — its CRLF bytes ARE the test.
tests/fixtures/format/valid/crlf.md -text
